@lang en

-- ===========================================================================
-- Income Tax Ordinance [New Version], ss 48 and 48A, the Area order of 5755-1995
-- and the foreign worker Regulations of 5775-2014.  Row IL-28.  NOUNS ONLY.
--
-- Sources (all deposited, all unofficial Wikisource consolidations; Hebrew is
-- authoritative; hashes in NOTES.md and SOURCE-LICENSE.md):
--   ITO = the Ordinance        ORD = the Area order of 5755-1995
--   REG = the Regulations of 5775-2014        FWL = the Foreign Workers Law 5751-1991
--
-- Every fact here is one a witness of ordinary competence could be asked about,
-- or a status a register records, or a choice of reading (Meng's SHRUG ruling of
-- 2026-10-08). Nothing here is a rule. The rules are in the three modules that
-- import this one.
-- ===========================================================================

§ `Ordinance ss 48 and 48A — the taxpayer`

-- Residence in the Area is one status per tax year, supplied by the caller
-- (fork F4, as row IL-01 forks it), unless the caller says it lasted for only
-- some months.
DECLARE `Residence in the Area over the tax year` IS ONE OF
    `the Area residence entered held for the whole tax year`
    `a resident of the Area for only part of the tax year` HAS
        -- a whole number from 1 to 11
        `the months of the tax year in which the taxpayer was a resident of the Area` IS A NUMBER

DECLARE Taxpayer HAS
    -- ITO line 202, ”שנת מס“: written as the calendar year in which the tax year begins.
    `the tax year`                                           IS A NUMBER

    -- ss 34 and 37 speak of a "יחיד" (an individual), as does s 36; a body of persons
    -- gets no credit point under any section this row encodes.
    `an individual`                                          IS A BOOLEAN

    -- s 36A speaks of an "אשה"; the Ordinance does not define it. An input convention (F9 of row IL-01).
    `a woman`                                                IS A BOOLEAN

    -- ITO s 1 "תושב ישראל", as determined by the caller for the tax year (row IL-08 encodes the test).
    `an Israeli resident in the tax year`                    IS A BOOLEAN

    -- ---- the facts s 48 reads through s 3A(a) (ITO lines 455-461) ----
    -- "תושב אזור": the s 1 residence test with "the Area" for "Israel", as the caller determines it.
    `a resident of the Area`                                 IS A BOOLEAN
    -- s 3A(a)(1): an Israeli citizen under the Citizenship Law 5712-1952.
    `an Israeli citizen under the Citizenship Law`           IS A BOOLEAN
    -- s 3A(a)(3): entitled to immigrate under the Law of Return 5710-1950 (counts only for a resident of the Area).
    `entitled to immigrate under the Law of Return`          IS A BOOLEAN
    `the taxpayer's residence in the Area over the tax year` IS A `Residence in the Area over the tax year`

    -- ---- the facts s 37 asks (ITO line 1600) ----
    -- "יחיד מוטב": the individual or the spouse reached retirement age, or is blind or disabled within s 9(5)(a) or (a1).
    `a favoured individual within section 37`                IS A BOOLEAN
    -- "שכלכלת בן זוגו היתה עליו".
    `the spouse's livelihood was upon the taxpayer`          IS A BOOLEAN
    -- "שהוכיח להנחת דעתו של פקיד השומה".
    `the taxpayer proved it to the assessor's satisfaction`  IS A BOOLEAN

    -- ---- fork F2 (s 36): income from personal exertion, as the caller determines it ----
    `the taxpayer had income from personal exertion in the tax year` IS A BOOLEAN

    -- ---- the facts the Foreign Workers Law and the Regulations ask ----
    -- FWL line 34, ”עובד זר“ – עובד שאינו אזרח ישראל, או תושב בה. "An Israeli citizen" is the Citizenship Law's
    -- (the field above); "a resident therein" is not defined in the FWL, an input.
    `a worker`                                               IS A BOOLEAN
    `a resident of Israel within the Foreign Workers Law`    IS A BOOLEAN
    -- REG 1, ”עובד זר“: holds a visa under s 2 of the Entry into Israel Law 5712-1952, or his stay or employment
    -- in Israel needs one.
    `holds a visa under section 2 of the Entry into Israel Law, or needs one` IS A BOOLEAN
    -- REG 2(1).
    `stay in Israel or the Area and employment there are permitted by law` IS A BOOLEAN
    -- REG 2(2): ”מומחה חוץ“ or ”מרצה אורח“ within the Regulations on stay expenses (1979, not deposited).
    `an expert from abroad or a guest lecturer`              IS A BOOLEAN
    -- REG 2(3): a visa and visit licence of type B/1 (temporary worker) under reg 5(a) of the Entry Regulations 5734-1974.
    `holds a B/1 temporary worker visa and licence`          IS A BOOLEAN
    -- REG 1, ”עובד זר חוקי בתחום הסיעוד“: a permit to work in the caring sector, and the stay extended under s 3A(b)
    -- of the Entry into Israel Law.
    `holds a permit to work in the caring sector`            IS A BOOLEAN
    `the stay is extended under section 3A(b) of the Entry into Israel Law` IS A BOOLEAN
    -- REG 3(c): "מספר החודשים שבהם שהה בארץ בשנת המס": whole months, 0 to 12, as the caller counts them.
    `the months of the tax year spent in Israel or the Area` IS A NUMBER
    -- REG 3(a), (a1), (b): the credits are taken in computing tax on income "לפי סעיף 2(1) או (2)".
    `the income taxed is income under section 2(1) or (2)`   IS A BOOLEAN

§ `Ordinance ss 48 and 48A — the provisions of Chapter Three`

-- ITO line 1559: Part C Chapter Three, ”פרק שלישי: ניכויים, זיכויים וקיצבאות ילדים“. The credit sections, and the two
-- deduction sections that are not credits. Repealed sections (35A, 42, 43, 45B, 46C, 47B) and sections that only
-- support another (33A, 40E, 41, 41A, 46A, 46B, 47C) are in NOTES.md's coverage table, not here.
DECLARE `A provision of Chapter Three` IS ONE OF
    `section 34`
    `section 35`
    `section 36`
    `section 36A`
    `section 37`
    `section 38`
    `section 39`
    `section 39A`
    `section 39B`
    `section 40`
    `section 40A`
    `section 40B`
    `section 40C`
    `section 40D`
    `section 44`
    `section 45`
    `section 45A`
    `section 46`
    `section 47, a deduction`
    `section 47A, a deduction`

DECLARE `What an instrument does to a provision` IS ONE OF
    `applies the provision as if the taxpayer were an Israeli resident`
    `gives the provision a partial effect, set out in the points`
    `disapplies the provision`
    `leaves the provision as the provision itself reads`

§ `Ordinance ss 48 and 48A — the credit points`

DECLARE `Credit points` HAS
    `the points under section 34`  IS A NUMBER
    `the points under section 36`  IS A NUMBER
    `the points under section 36A` IS A NUMBER
    `the points under section 37`  IS A NUMBER

DECLARE `Which instrument reaches the taxpayer` IS ONE OF
    `neither instrument reaches the taxpayer`
    `the Area order reaches the taxpayer`
    `the foreign worker regulations reach the taxpayer`

§ `Ordinance ss 48 and 48A — the readings (Meng's ruling SHRUG, 2026-10-08)`

-- Where the text is silent or two readings are arguable and they give different
-- answers, one named switch, default DECLINE. NOTES.md, fork register.

-- F1 (carried from row IL-01): does s 36A, which has no residence limb, give
-- its half point to a woman who is not an Israeli resident?
DECLARE `A reading of section 36A on residence` IS ONE OF
    `section 36A has no residence condition`
    `section 36A gives its half point only to an Israeli resident`
    `declined where residence decides section 36A`

-- F2 (carried from row IL-01): s 36's heading speaks of travel to the place of earning.
DECLARE `A reading of section 36 on income from personal exertion` IS ONE OF
    `section 36 for every individual`
    `section 36 only for an individual with income from personal exertion`
    `declined where income from personal exertion decides section 36`

-- F4 (carried from row IL-01, for the Area order): a resident of the Area for only part of the tax year.
DECLARE `A reading of sections 34 and 36 for part of a tax year in the Area` IS ONE OF
    `one residence status for the whole tax year`
    `apportioned by the months of residence, as section 41 apportions`
    `declined for residence in part of a tax year`

-- FW1: do the cited sections' own residence conditions still bind a foreign worker whom the Regulations
-- give "points under ss 34, 36 and 36A"?
DECLARE `A reading of the foreign worker regulations on the cited sections' conditions` IS ONE OF
    `the regulations give their points without the cited sections' residence conditions`
    `the cited sections' own residence conditions still apply`
    `declined where the cited sections' residence conditions decide`

-- FW2: tax years 2002 to 2014, after s 48A was enacted and before the Regulations apply (REG 4).
DECLARE `A reading of the tax years from 2002 to 2014 under section 48A` IS ONE OF
    `no instrument under section 48A applied before the regulations of 5775-2014`
    `declined for the tax years from 2002 to 2014`

-- FW3: REG 3(d) disapplies "the provisions of Chapter Three" without the limit to credits that s 48A's power has.
DECLARE `A reading of regulation 3(d) on the chapter's deductions` IS ONE OF
    `regulation 3(d) reaches the whole chapter as it is written`
    `regulation 3(d) reaches credits only, which is all the power of section 48A gives`
    `declined where regulation 3(d) and the chapter's deductions meet`

-- OV: a person whom both instruments reach.
DECLARE `A reading of a foreign worker who is also an Area resident who is not an Israeli citizen` IS ONE OF
    `the foreign worker regulations prevail`
    `the Area order prevails`
    `declined where the order and the regulations both reach the taxpayer`

DECLARE `The readings of the forks of row IL-28` HAS
    `fork F1, section 36A and residence`                      IS A `A reading of section 36A on residence`
    `fork F2, section 36 and income from personal exertion`   IS A `A reading of section 36 on income from personal exertion`
    `fork F4, residence in the Area for part of a tax year`   IS A `A reading of sections 34 and 36 for part of a tax year in the Area`
    `fork FW1, the cited sections' conditions`                IS A `A reading of the foreign worker regulations on the cited sections' conditions`
    `fork FW2, the tax years from 2002 to 2014`               IS A `A reading of the tax years from 2002 to 2014 under section 48A`
    `fork FW3, regulation 3(d) and deductions`                IS A `A reading of regulation 3(d) on the chapter's deductions`
    `fork OV, both instruments reach the taxpayer`            IS A `A reading of a foreign worker who is also an Area resident who is not an Israeli citizen`
